NAME
	history-svc (service) - sample every numeric file in a directory once a minute into day-long ring files that keep their history across restarts

INTERFACE
	service (MatrixService)

READS
	<mount>/<file>	each file directly in the mount whose content
			starts with a number (envsrv(4)'s temp,
			humidity and pressure, or any other); files
			that are not numbers are passed over.

WRITES
	<file>/history	ring: ts value, oldest first, ts in seconds
			since the epoch; the last 1440 samples (24 h)
	<file>/current	the last value read

DESCRIPTION
	The first sample is taken at start, then one every 60 s, the
	value kept as the file wrote it.  At init the history files
	already in the outdir are read back, so a composition loaded
	again, or an emulator started again, keeps the day it had
	(/tmp/matrix is on the host's disk); a file that has gone keeps
	its history, and samples not taken leave a gap in time, which
	line-plot draws as a gap.  The clock is read in init and carried
	on by the millisecond counter, as the service runs with no /dev.
	Files are replaced atomically (tmp file + rename).

SEE ALSO
	line-plot, sparkline (draw the history files)
	envsrv(4) (a sensor's readings as such a directory)
